  {
    "id": "wh-383493",
    "source": "wowhead",
    "dateRaw": "Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:00:00 -0500",
    "author": "Wowhead Staff",
    "category": "Live",
    "badgeColor": "border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-950/80 text-amber-300",
    "title": {
      "en": "\"Phantom Damage\" Bug from Melee Attacks Fixed",
      "es": "Se ha corregido el error \"Phantom DaMago\" de los ataques cuerpo a cuerpo"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "\"Phantom Damage\" Bug from Melee Attacks Fixed...",
      "es": "Se ha corregido el error \"Phantom DaMago\" de los ataques cuerpo a cuerpo..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ad792a48131e9.44754527\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">With the release of Patch 12.1.5, the long-standing \"Phantom Damage\" bug from melee attacks was fixed.<br><br>About a week ago, we <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/all-melee-swings-cause-phantom-damage-to-health-bars-in-midnight-383363\" data-contiguous=\"true\">previously covered</a> a bug with the UI. When a player took damage from melee swings, the UI showed your health changing by double the amount before rebounding and correcting itself to the correct value. For example, if you took a 100k hit, you would see your health bar lose 200k for a split second before it corrected to a 100k hit. Many players who saw this happen in Delves thought Valeera was just landing a really well-timed heal on them. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><video controls=\"\" poster=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1305381-damage-bug.jpg?maxWidth=800\" preload=\"metadata\" style=\"width: 800px;\"><source src=\"https://nether.wowhead.com/video-stream/440281-damage-bug?dataEnv=1&amp;locale=0\"></video></div><br><br>This bug has been around since The War Within, with some reports of it being in Dragonflight. One of the biggest problems with this bug is that it could cause a lot of panic when your health drops super low, but you're really at half health. Good news, though: this bug has been fixed!<br><br>Performing the same test as before, you can now see no extra damage or rebounding on the health bar or raid frames. This appears very crisp compared to what a lot of people probably got used to. <br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><video controls=\"\" style=\"width: 800px;\"><source src=\"https://nether.wowhead.com/video-stream/441505-phantom-daamge?dataEnv=1&amp;locale=0\"></video></div><br><br>With the <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/murder-row-boss-deals-fake-damage-to-players-383347\" data-contiguous=\"true\">fake damage</a> of Murder Row and <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/all-melee-swings-cause-phantom-damage-to-health-bars-in-midnight-383363\" data-contiguous=\"true\">phantom damage</a> of melee swings now fixed, hopefully this is the last of any bugs that show incorrect information to players about their health bars.</div>\n            \n            <noscript>With the release of Patch 12.1.5, the long-standing &quot;Phantom Damage&quot; bug from melee attacks was fixed.<br /><br />About a week ago, we <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/all-melee-swings-cause-phantom-damage-to-health-bars-in-midnight-383363\">previously covered</a> a bug with the UI. When a player took damage from melee swings, the UI showed your health changing by double the amount before rebounding and correcting itself to the correct value. For example, if you took a 100k hit, you would see your health bar lose 200k for a split second before it corrected to a 100k hit. Many players who saw this happen in Delves thought Valeera was just landing a really well-timed heal on them. <br /><br />This bug has been around since The War Within, with some reports of it being in Dragonflight. One of the biggest problems with this bug is that it could cause a lot of panic when your health drops super low, but you're really at half health. Good news, though: this bug has been fixed!<br /><br />Performing the same test as before, you can now see no extra damage or rebounding on the health bar or raid frames. This appears very crisp compared to what a lot of people probably got used to. <br /><br />With the <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/murder-row-boss-deals-fake-damage-to-players-383347\">fake damage</a> of Murder Row and <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/all-melee-swings-cause-phantom-damage-to-health-bars-in-midnight-383363\">phantom damage</a> of melee swings now fixed, hopefully this is the last of any bugs that show incorrect information to players about their health bars.</noscript>            \n        ",
    "imageUrl": "https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/blog/images/55827-phantom-damage-bug-from-melee-attacks-fixed.jpg",
